    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0699" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/127: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-17T16:00:00+01:00">January 17, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 19—6:30]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Consulate’s 21, January 16, 10 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Italians are making every effort to have the Abyssinians withdraw
                        their invocation of the Covenant. Avenol<anchor n="6" xml:id="d470-f1"/>
                        stated to the Abyssinian delegate that the Italians had informed him that
                        they would regard a bringing of the matter before the Council while direct
                        negotiations were in progress as prejudicial to a friendly
                        settlement.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Abyssinians do not consider that the present direct conversations
                        constitute negotiations in any acceptable sense and are standing upon their
                        appeal. In this they are acting under instructions.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d470-f1" n="6" xml:id="d470-f1-content">
                <p>Joseph L. A. Avenol, Secretary General of the League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
